OL,3,GNEWSAWhen whole towns closed and headed
OL,4,Afor the seaside
OL,5,
OL,6,FNot so long ago, many towns and cities
OL,7,Fin Britain would virtually close down
OL,8,Ffor a couple of weeks each summer, with
OL,9,Ftheir people rushing for the amusement
OL,10,Farcades and fresh air of the seaside.
OL,12,FIt was as much of a beloved fixture in
OL,13,Fthe calendar as Christmas.
OL,15,FAs one person told a BBC film crew in
OL,16,F1957: "It was a bit lonely if you
OL,17,Fweren't going away. The local shops,
OL,18,Feven the market, used to be shut for
OL,19,Ftwo weeks as well."
